    "readout_text": "To evaluate the expression:\n\n$$\n2^3 - 1^3 + 4^3 - 3^3 + 6^3 - 5^3 + \\dots + 18^3 - 17^3\n$$\n\nwe observe that the expression alternates between the cube of even numbers and the cube of the preceding odd numbers. This pattern can be expressed as a sum of pairs of the form:\n\n$$\n(2n)^3 - (2n - 1)^3\n$$\n\nfor $ n = 1 $ to $ 9 $, since the last term is $ 18^3 - 17^3 $, and $ 2n = 18 \\Rightarrow n = 9 $.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Simplify the General Term\n\nWe expand the general term:\n\n$$\n(2n)^3 - (2n - 1)^3\n$$\n\nUsing the binomial expansion:\n\n$$\n(2n)^3 = 8n^3\n$$\n$$\n(2n - 1)^3 = 8n^3 - 12n^2 + 6n - 1\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n(2n)^3 - (2n - 1)^3 = 12n^2 - 6n + 1\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Sum the Simplified Expression\n\nNow, we sum this expression over $ n = 1 $ to $ 9 $:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n=1}^{9} (12n^2 - 6n + 1) = 12 \\sum_{n=1}^{9} n^2 - 6 \\sum_{n=1}^{9} n + \\sum_{n=1}^{9} 1\n$$\n\nWe use standard summation formulas:\n\n- $ \\sum_{n=1}^{9} n = \\frac{9 \\cdot 10}{2} = 45 $\n- $ \\sum_{n=1}^{9} n^2 = \\frac{9 \\cdot 10 \\cdot 19}{6} = 285 $\n- $ \\sum_{n=1}^{9} 1 = 9 $\n\nSubstitute into the expression:\n\n$$\n12 \\cdot 285 - 6 \\cdot 45 + 9 = 3420 - 270 + 9 = 3159\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Verification via Direct Computation\n\nTo confirm, we can compute each pair explicitly:\n\n- $ 2^3 - 1^3 = 8 - 1 = 7 $\n- $ 4^3 - 3^3 = 64 - 27 = 37 $\n- $ 6^3 - 5^3 = 216 - 125 = 91 $\n- $ 8^3 - 7^3 = 512 - 343 = 169 $\n- $ 10^3 - 9^3 = 1000 - 729 = 271 $\n- $ 12^3 - 11^3 = 1728 - 1331 = 397 $\n- $ 14^3 - 13^3 = 2744 - 2197 = 547 $\n- $ 16^3 - 15^3 = 4096 - 3375 = 721 $\n- $ 18^3 - 17^3 = 5832 - 4913 = 919 $\n\nSumming these values:\n\n$$\n7 + 37 + 91 + 169 + 271 + 397 + 547 + 721 + 919 = 3159\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Conclusion\n\nAll methods—algebraic simplification, summation formulas, and direct computation—yield the same result.\n\n$$\n\\boxed{3159}\n$$\n\n\\confidence{Almost certain}",
